msgid "Check a DosCo folder"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Read a DosCo folder against the documents of the active graph with "
"Resources.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The **DosCo** (the documentary corpus of an Extended Matrix study) is the"
" folder where the files of the documents are kept, each named after its "
"document: ``D.01 plan.jpg``, ``D.02_section.pdf``, ``D.14-survey.png``. "
"The name starts with the EM id of the document (``D.`` and a number), "
"followed by a space, an underscore or a hyphen. Reading the folder "
"against the graph shows which files have no document in the graph yet, "
"and turns them into documents."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the graph whose documents you want to check: the folder is always "
"read against the active graph, and its name is shown at the top of the "
"window. The folder is read by EMStudio's service: on the desktop the "
"service of this computer, on the web the node's."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read the folder"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose ``Tools ▸ Resources``. The window **Resources** opens; the line "
"beside its title names the graph it reads against, and its **▾** changes "
"it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The same window opens, with the folder already filled in and read, from "
"**Scan as DosCo…**: in the **Files** window, open a folder, choose "
"nothing, and find the button in the **Info** tab among the gestures of "
"the folder. An empty **Shelf** offers it too, for the ``DosCo`` folder of"
" the study."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In **DosCo folder**, write the full path of the folder, for example the "
"``DosCo`` folder beside ``TempluMare.em.json``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Press **Read the folder**."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The status line says how many files are not yet a document, and three "
"lists fill the window."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Files not yet a document**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The files of the folder whose EM id is not a document of the graph. Each "
"row has a preview, the file name and its EM id. Above the list, two notes"
" report what the reading leaves out: the files without an EM id, and, "
"marked **▲**, an EM id carried by more than one file."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Documents of the graph**"
msgstr ""

msgid "The documents the graph already has, with their previews."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Resources of the graph**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The resources of the graph, each with where its file is: **a file of this"
" computer**, **a web address** or **on the room's server**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Files named with an extractor's id (``D.02.01``) or a combiner's "
"(``C.3``) are not listed, because those nodes are made in the graph, not "
"from a file."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The reading writes a small index, ``.em_resources_manifest.json``, inside"
" the folder. It gives each file a stable identity that survives the next "
"readings, and EM Tools in Blender reads the same index."
msgstr ""

msgid "Make the missing documents"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In **Files not yet a document**, press **→ Document** on a row. A "
"document with that EM id as its name is created in the active graph, and "
"the row leaves the list."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Select the new document in the **Outliner** and complete it in the "
"**Inspector**: its description, its date, its licence (see "
":doc:`/reference/inspector`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To bring files in as documents with their date and licence at once, use "
"*Porta dentro* instead (see :doc:`porta-dentro`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Copy a file to the room's server"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In **Resources of the graph**, a resource whose file is on this computer "
"has the button **Copy to the server**. It copies the file to the room's "
"server with the same identity, and the resource's address becomes the "
"copy on the server. The graph keeps pointing at the same resource. When "
"the server cannot take files, the message says why and the resource stays"
" as it was."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"After a change in the folder, press **Read the folder** again to bring "
"the lists up to date. **Done** closes the window."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`porta-dentro`, to bring files in as documents."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/how-to/sources/documents-and-media`, to read and describe the "
"documents."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/how-to/files/find-missing-files`, when the graph cites files that "
"have moved."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`/how-to/rooms/bring-a-file-into-a-room`, for rooms."
msgstr ""

